WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.210
Everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start!

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.980
When watching Kaleido Star,
please keep the room brightly lit,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.640
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.720
I'm Sora Naegino.
I came to America all by myself

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.420
with aspirations of joining Kaleido Stage.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.190
Everything is new to me,

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.690
but I'm doing my best in the spirit of
"try it rather than think about it."

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.060
There's nothing I can't do if I try

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.860
and if I can do it without trying,
I'd be super lucky.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.920
And if I'm gonna do it, I just gotta do it!
Gotta! Gotta! That's me.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.540
Well, well, well, do you know
anyone who's difficult?

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.160
Rosetta seems to be just that kind of person.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.670
She's a talented diabolo performer,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.440
but I end up performing with her on stage.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.010
But wait, I've never worked
with diabolo before.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:48.510
Oh boy, what should I do? What? What?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.160
<i>What is it that you want to do?</i>

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.160
<i>Yaritai koto wa nani</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.830
<i>Every time I was asked that</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.830
<i>Sou kikareru tabi</i>

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.560
<i>I looked up at the blue sky</i>

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.560
<i>Aoi sora miageta</i>

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.580
<i>The answer is only in my heart</i>

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.580
<i>Kotae wa only my heart</i>

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:25.090
<i>I don't easily say the words
that are really important</i>

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:25.090
<i>Honto ni daiji na kotoba wa
kantan ni wa iwanai</i>

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:32.390
<i>I start running towards the place
the light points to</i>

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:32.390
<i>Hikari ga yubisasu basho e to hashiridasu yo</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:40.340
<i>There's so much in my heart that I want
to embrace, I could cry</i>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:40.340
<i>Dakishimetai mono nara
nakitai hodo mune ni aru</i>

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:47.310
<i>I'll keep painting my way, I promise,
take it someday</i>

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:47.310
<i>Egakitsuzukete yuku kitto
take it someday</i>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:55.280
<i>Beyond the horizon, where
the white clouds drift</i>

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:55.280
<i>Shiroi kumo ga nagareru
chiheisen no mukou ni</i>

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:07.020
<i>The future is lined up and
it'll always be there by my side</i>

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:07.020
<i>Naranderu mirai wa itsumo soba ni aru kara</i>

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.610
Jonathan, this way!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.810
So this is Jonathan's pool?

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.710
This is how it turned out after
I followed Kalos' request.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.510
I'm glad that Jonathan seems to like it.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.790
It's great, it's great!

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.320
It's so big.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.430
He looks happy.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.530
Jonathan, over here!

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.400
Jonathan!

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.280
He's ignoring us.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.330
Ungrateful.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.040
I guess I won't be able to be with him
all the time anymore.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.550
Marion, Vince is back from the market.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.710
Your meal is here, Jonathan.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:15.720
Vince, Jonathan says he's tired of waiting!

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:21.960
That girl...

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:26.410
The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.580
The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.580
"The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile"

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.210
The Amazing Girl Who Doesn't Smile

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.820
Okay, Rosetta.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.580
Your provisional contract is one week.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.920
After you finish tonight's performance,

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.350
we'll do a formal contract including
an extension of your time here.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.150
I hope you understand these arrangements.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.500
Rosetta?

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.030
The French diabolo prodigy
performer is finally here.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.670
That's right.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.890
She's really a genius!

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.240
I'm a fan of hers, so I couldn't help it.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.210
Sora.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.280
What are you doing?

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.980
We're just passing by.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.350
We weren't eavesdropping or anything.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:04.750
He's not going to buy it.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:04.750
We weren't eavesdropping or anything.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:05.540
He's not going to buy it.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.310
Sora, come in for a second.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.210
Yes?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.580
Boss wants to ask you to be
a guide for the guest.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:13.810
Really?

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.220
This is Sora Naegino.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.830
She will take you to your room.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.190
You should rest a little.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.830
I'm Sora Naegino, nice to meet you.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.300
See you later then.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.460
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.370
Um, well, I'm your fan...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.570
Nice to meet you.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:30.640
I'm Mia.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.700
I'm Anna.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.030
Nice to meet you.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.440
Where is Layla Hamilton?

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.940
She's not in yet.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.250
I see.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.780
Your baggage has already been
delivered to the dormitory.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.990
I'll take you there.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.450
Let's go, Rosetta.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.150
Oh, Boss.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.720
Thank you for building
a big pool for Jonathan.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.760
This is your room, Rosetta!

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.070
The sea breeze is nice,
so I'll keep the windows open, okay?

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:08.510
Sora?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:09.570
Huh? What?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.440
So Kalos only arranged a regular room
for me like the ones you have?

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.020
Huh?

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.920
I was the youngest winner in the
world diabolo competition

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.520
and I won the next four years straight.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.330
That's right, I remember watching you on TV

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.960
when you were the youngest
to win the competition.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.630
You were answering TV interviewers
so actively despite being so young.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.570
That's why I remember it so well.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.140
Traveling around the world from one
circus to another all by herself,

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.940
a French born genius child
performer of diabolo!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.410
That's Belgium.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.410
a French born genius child
performer of diabolo!

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.100
That's Belgium.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.830
I was born in Belgium and
studied in France.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.380
You're supposed to be my guide,

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.610
but you don't know
anything about me, do you?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.910
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.220
How was it, Sora?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.260
It's finally come to Kaleido Stage,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:05.430
the super diabolo performed
by world champion Rosetta!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.370
If you want to be a world champion yourself,

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.810
you can get your own diabolo at our
gift shop starting at $30.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.180
Miss Rosetta!

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.610
Excuse us.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:22.410
We want you to like, teach us diabolo.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.920
My agreement with my agent
does not allow me

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.720
to display my diabolo performance
except on stage.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:28.960
Please shut the door.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.860
I can't concentrate.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.690
I'm sorry.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.530
How rude!

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.050
It's like, poor little me.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:04.560
That girl is amazing.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.690
She's a genius.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.460
She's amazing.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.690
But I wonder why?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.760
It's not that fun to watch.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.330
She's like a well-oiled diabolo machine.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.540
Mom, I'm bored.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.530
A clown's coming on stage after this, okay?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.790
It's time for an intermission now. Oh!

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.860
Welcome to Kaleido Stage.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:45.770
Miss Layla, how was my performance?

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.470
It was perfect.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.240
There were no mistakes.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.170
Thank you.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.160
I'll enjoy your show for the week.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.530
I'm sure I can be with you longer than that.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.210
It sounds like you're quite confident.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.680
Oh, yes.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.670
Rosetta, I need to talk to you.
Can you spare a minute?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.640
About the contract extension, right?

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:04.790
No.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.150
Today is your last performance.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.120
What?

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:11.580
Maybe I should have picked something
more suited for a younger audience?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.060
As for the pay, I will pay you one
week's worth as agreed in the contract.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.050
But you don't need to
appear on stage anymore.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.970
Well, everyone, it's almost time to start!

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:23.470
I demand a satisfactory explanation
from you in the dressing room!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.680
I'm going just for a while.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.400
Sora, it's almost our turn!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.250
Rosetta, your diabolo is wonderful.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.410
That's why I invited you.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:39.550
However, the audience at Kaleido Stage
did not enjoy your diabolo.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:43.220
I realized that when
I watched your show today.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.620
Then I'll rearrange the diabolo combinations.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:48.760
Rosetta, I'm sorry, but...

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.460
I didn't make any mistakes!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.390
It was a perfect performance.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.700
They don't enjoy my diabolo

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.330
because the audience at Kaleido Stage
isn't sophisticated enough!

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.940
So you are saying that it's the
audience's fault?

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.570
You believe you're right and
you can stay the way you are?

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.450
I'm a world champion.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.580
The world recognizes my diabolo skills.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.280
Kaleido Stage exists to
entertain the audience.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.960
And the audience was not
enjoying your performance.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.160
Why can't they enjoy my performance?

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.860
Kaleido Stage is not an athletic event
to show off your skills.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.600
Oh, excuse me.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.040
I will talk to your agent.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.340
Ken, when you have time, take Rosetta
and show her around Marine Park.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.310
But, Boss...

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.710
Don't treat me like I'm stupid!

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:41.920
Rosetta!

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:42.450
What?

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.080
How should I know?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.110
What's going on?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.450
What's wrong with her?

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.650
She runs fast too.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.790
Boss, you're really not going to
allow her on stage?

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:55.030
Of course.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.260
That was not a show.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.660
But it's only after one show...

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.400
Watching it once was enough.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.700
You don't know that.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.880
She may be able to change.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.650
I won't mind bringing Rosetta
back on stage, but...

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:21.320
Oh, really?

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.850
You have to be with her.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:23.980
What?

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.490
Excuse me?

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:28.530
The contract is for six more days.

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:30.230
During that period, you do what you can

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.300
to get her back on the stage.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.000
Well, that is to say...

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:34.540
See you later.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:35.240
Oh, wait.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:38.140
Act two of Cinderella will be starting shortly!

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:38.770
Oh, no! Let's hurry, Sora!

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:39.510
I've never done diabolo before.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:39.510
Oh, no! Let's hurry, Sora!

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.670
I've never done diabolo before.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:46.310
It's a crucial time for you right now.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:49.110
My performance is always perfect.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.290
When you were little, that was enough
for you to get plenty of attention,

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.020
but the number of jobs
has decreased recently.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.550
You have to change a little.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.890
Hang in there for a little longer.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:10:59.860
All right?

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.460
But I'm performing flawlessly...

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:07.130
Are you all right, Sora?

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:08.290
Not at all.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.240
Why don't you just tell him that
you can't do it?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.670
Yeah, why don't you?

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.440
Oh, but I'll still give it a try.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:14.930
Of course, you will.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:23.620
Oh! Oh! Miss Sarah! Miss Sarah!
We have a problem!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.790
What's wrong?

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:26.690
Rosetta's not here!

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:27.990
Oh, my, that IS a problem.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.860
I wonder if she left for home?

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.130
At this time?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.930
Rosetta! Rosetta!

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:35.800
Rosetta!

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:38.670
Oh, really! Where did you go?!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.730
Rosetta! Rosetta!

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.370
Oh, Sora, she's right here!

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.370
Rosetta! Rosetta!

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:43.360
What?!

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:48.470
I'm so glad.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.810
Why does Kalos want me to pair up with you?

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.190
Do you really think you can do it?

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:06.880
I'm planning on trying first,
rather than thinking about it.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:09.000
You know, if you start thinking,

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.230
you only worry about things like
what if you make a mistake.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.840
I don't think it makes for a fun show.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.200
We should always expect ourselves
to perform flawlessly.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.710
It's better not to do it
than to make mistakes.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.810
There's no way I can perform like you do.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:24.610
So I want them to at least enjoy it.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:28.750
Or rather, maybe it's about trying hard
than being perfect.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.350
Working hard?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.390
Ken!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:34.050
I got these for you. I thought they
could be useful.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.420
Look.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:38.530
Wow! Where did you get these?

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.560
We stocked up too many.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.430
I was wondering what to do with all these.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:43.620
It's my fault, isn't it?

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.570
Sorry, I didn't mean it like that.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.400
The audience didn't enjoy my show.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:50.500
That's all.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.560
Sorry, Rosetta. Sorry...

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.940
In the end, maybe I can't...

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.670
I don't think it's your fault.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:57.880
What?

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:01.480
She was nine years old
when she won the world championship,

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.420
but if I remember correctly,
she started diabolo when she was five.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:08.360
At that age, I just loved Kaleido Stage
and enjoyed watching it

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.190
without thinking about anything else.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:11.920
Me too.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:16.060
She might never have had a chance
to enjoy the show as the audience.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.160
Ken, I'm going to give it a try.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:38.780
To the airport.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.390
She's gone.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.590
Okay.

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:47.390
Oh, Ken?

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.960
A show that's not perfect, but still
entertaining? What is that?

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.300
Miss, do you know the people on that bike?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.340
They've been following us the whole way.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:14.210
What's wrong?

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.060
Sora wants you to see her show.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.260
Why do I have to?

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.490
You have to see it.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.210
Go, Jonathan!

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.150
Catch! What is this?!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.280
It's a fish.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.770
It's a saurel! Saurel!

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.770
You're doing good, Jonathan!

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:47.750
Give it back to me!

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.860
Give it back, Jonathan!

00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:57.190
Rosetta! Here, hurry!

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.290
I'm just going to take a quick look. Oh!

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.400
Sora, jump in!

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.100
I did it!

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.020
Sora, you're awful!

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.750
Jonathan's better than you!

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:21.650
Jonathan!

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.090
Wait!

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:26.620
Hey, Jonathan! Hold it right there!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.730
You're doing good, Jonathan!

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:30.160
Sora, go!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:33.100
You! There! I did it!

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.500
Look!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.340
You're awesome!

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:37.530
You did great!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.910
Sora, go for it!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.030
Sora!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.440
Isn't it strange?

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:43.470
Huh?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.410
When I'm watching Sora's show,
it makes me nervous,

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.450
because I'm worried
she's going to make a mistake.

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:49.920
Here!

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.090
She does, in fact, make mistakes,

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:52.550
but once in a while,
she can be incredibly wonderful.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.350
Oh, where are you, Jonathan?

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.350
but once in a while,
she can be incredibly wonderful.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:58.320
Unbelievable, like magic.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:02.930
Please watch Sora's performance today.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.150
Sora's performance?

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:09.960
Here!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:13.360
Yeah!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.490
Amazing...

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.250
It's completely different from my show.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.020
Sora...

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.730
Sora.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:46.060
Rosetta! You came to see the show!

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:50.740
I want to see what our diabolo
performance might look like together.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.270
Me too.

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:56.980
Okay.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.890
You'll do it perfectly,
while I try really hard at it.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:04.020
Don't you think that'll be interesting?

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:06.190
That's a good idea.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:11.160
But to do that, Sora's diabolo needs
to improve a little more.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.900
Instead of thinking, I'll just try it!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.500
Wrong!

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.600
Okay!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.500
Do it as if you're going toward the diabolo!

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.380
Don't actually collide with it.

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:25.780
Okay.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.580
The upright Devil.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.320
It means that she needs to make
extreme efforts.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.390
Again!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.390
It means that she needs to make
extreme efforts.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.320
Okay.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.320
It means that she needs to make
extreme efforts.

00:17:41.130 --> 00:17:42.400
Not good. One more time!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.330
Okay.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.830
Reading Tarot cards by myself
only makes me feel empty.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:53.340
This... this... this is really tough!

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.440
Only one more day left until the time limit.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.140
We don't have time to goof off!

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.210
Looks like they've managed
to make the deadline.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:05.150
Building a new set in
such a hurry was tough.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.120
Sorry.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.320
Well, I think it's an interesting idea.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.020
Did you say it was their idea?

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.190
Yeah.

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:12.950
They make a good team.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:18.970
Now, at last, it's time for the first
diabolo battle in history!

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.400
In this corner, the world diabolo champion,

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.920
Rosetta!

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.440
In the other corner, with five days of
diabolo experience,

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:25.200
Sora!

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:28.880
Now, let's see the long awaited
outcome of this battle!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.140
Ready?

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.440
Start!

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:54.920
Okay!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:09.280
Doing good! Go, Sora!

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:11.010
Rosetta, don't lose!

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:14.850
Here!

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:17.990
Go!

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:19.460
Not so fast!

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.900
Ouch! Shoot!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.180
Rosetta made a mistake!

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:44.150
I can't believe this!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.770
Winner, Rosetta!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.970
Champion!

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:23.720
They did it.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.160
You're amazing, Sora.

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.330
Awesome!

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.880
Bravo! Bravo!

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:30.490
You changed Rosetta, Sora.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.860
Sora, I remember back when
I was nine years old

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.700
and competing in the world championship.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:41.440
Everyone was smiling
behind the interviewers.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.340
Everyone was saying, "It was fun,"
or, "It was interesting."

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.740
Everyone was happy.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.710
Back then, I really felt glad
I was doing diabolo.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:55.550
I completely forgot how happy
I was during that time.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:59.120
The time when I loved diabolo so much.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:01.090
I remembered it today.

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:03.590
Thanks to Kaleido Stage

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.300
and thanks to you, Sora.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.130
Wait a sec, Rosetta.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:11.140
Wow... Wow...

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.310
What? What?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.540
I owe it to you, Sora.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.510
What?

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.310
Thanks to your magic, Sora.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.770
Wow...

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.530
So you're going home after all?

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.190
Yes. Thank you, Sora.

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.820
Yesterday's show was successful
because of your talent.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.760
It was very captivating.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.060
Oh...

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:43.230
No, I owe it all to Kaleido Stage.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:46.510
I really would have liked to
extend the contract.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:47.530
I can't.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.870
Is this your revenge for what
happened a week ago?

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:54.310
I want to go home and develop
my own diabolo over again.

00:21:56.050 --> 00:21:59.550
Boss, you look like your girlfriend
just broke up with you.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.320
Yeah, that's what I feel like.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:06.920
See you again, Rosetta!

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:14.160
Merci, Sora.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:25.010
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:25.010
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.410
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.410
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:27.410 --> 00:22:30.320
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:27.410 --> 00:22:30.320
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.620
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.620
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:37.420
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:37.420
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:42.060
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:42.060
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:46.770
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:46.770
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:51.470
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:51.470
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.640
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.640
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:58.310
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:58.310
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:02.980
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:02.980
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:09.460
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:09.460
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:14.830
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:14.830
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.600
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:24.970
You have that much commercial value.

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:28.340
And so, Miss Layla's father came to
Kaleido Stage,

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:30.480
but he left without seeing her show.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:33.450
It seems he sees his daughter as
nothing more than a business tool.

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:35.640
Even on her birthday, he tried to get
away with it by just spending money.

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:39.450
So we'll just have to make her birthday
party a success all by ourselves!

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:41.080
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:43.360
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times"

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.790
An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.790
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times"

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.560
An Amazing Star Even In Tough Times

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.560
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...
